cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you reference Vega in written work, please cite it as below.
title: "Vega: an encrypted messenger with no server"
abstract: >-
  A peer-to-peer encrypted messenger with no server component. Identity is
  self-certifying — an account id is the hash of an Ed25519 public key — and
  device rosters are published as hash-linked signed logs that any contact
  verifies offline. Messages use the Olm double ratchet inside a sealed-sender
  layer, and travel over a ladder of transports that degrades from the local
  network through DHT rendezvous and peer relaying to offline mailboxes, with no
  node able to read what it carries.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/guhhammer/vega
authors:
  # An entity rather than a person: this project is cited by its name.
  - name: The Vega contributors
keywords:
  - end-to-end encryption
  - peer-to-peer
  - decentralised
  - messaging
  - libp2p
  - double ratchet
